Starting with the 10 days of ansible challenge 
Day 1/10 – Starting my Ansible Journey
Configuration management is one of the most powerful parts of DevOps.
Instead of manually logging into servers and running commands, Ansible lets us automate everything with simple YAML playbooks.
✨ What I learned today:
• Ansible is agentless – it works over SSH
• Uses YAML playbooks to define tasks
• Great for configuration management and automation
Quick example:
Run command:
ansible all -m ping
Dry Run (Check Mode):
ansible-playbook install_nginx.yml --check
Check mode lets you see what will change without actually changing anything.
Safe automation = Happy DevOps 
